      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, my tomato plants are acting weird. the leaves at the bottom are turning yellow but the ones at the top look okay. what do you think is going on and how can i fix the soil?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing lower leaves on tomatoes usually points to a nitrogen deficiency, since the plant moves nitrogen to the new growth at the top. It can also be a sign of overwatering or a magnesium shortage. For the soil, work in a balanced organic fertilizer (like compost or a 5-5-5 blend) and check drainage—if the soil stays soggy, mix in perlite or coarse sand. Also, a foliar spray of diluted Epsom salt (1 tbsp per gallon) can help if it’s magnesium. Water only when the top inch of soil is dry.",
